<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>title</key>
    <string>Download Progress</string>
    <key>items</key>
    <array>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSGroupCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Download Progress (Experimental)</string>
        <key>footerText</key>
        <string>Shows the Island as a progress bar with the downloaded size, the total size and the speed while something downloads. Off by default. Early feature: the built-in test download and App Store downloads (switch below) work so far. Browser downloads come later.</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSwitchCell</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <false/>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadProgressEnabled</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Show Download Progress</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSGroupCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>App Store Downloads (Experimental)</string>
        <key>footerText</key>
        <string>Shows an App Store download as it happens (a new install; updates and TestFlight are not confirmed yet). iOS only reports a percentage for these, so you get the bar, the percentage and an estimate of the time left, not sizes or speed. Needs Show Download Progress above. Off by default.</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSwitchCell</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <false/>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadAppStoreEnabled</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Show App Store Downloads</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSGroupCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Look</string>
        <key>footerText</key>
        <string>Minimal draws its own pill: a header with the app and file name, the downloaded size above the bar, the total below it, the speed on the left and the percentage on the right. Detailed is the system's expanded Island with the name and one line of text under a bar.</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSLinkListCell</string>
        <key>detail</key>
        <string>PSListItemsController</string>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadProgressStyle</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Style</string>
        <key>validTitles</key>
        <array>
          <string>Minimal</string>
          <string>Detailed</string>
        </array>
        <key>validValues</key>
        <array>
          <integer>0</integer>
          <integer>1</integer>
        </array>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSGroupCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Minimal Size</string>
        <key>footerText</key>
        <string>The Minimal pill finds the Island and sits over it, with the Island's own height kept clear at its top. Width is the pill's width (it is never narrower than the Island plus a margin), Bottom padding is the space under the content, and Move up or down nudges it from the Island's top. Changes apply while the pill is showing, so start a test download and adjust.</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSliderCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Width</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <real>296.0</real>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadPillWidth</string>
        <key>min</key>
        <real>200.0</real>
        <key>max</key>
        <real>380.0</real>
        <key>showValue</key>
        <true/>
        <key>valueFormat</key>
        <string>%.0f pt</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSliderCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Bottom padding</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <real>10.0</real>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadPillBottomPadding</string>
        <key>min</key>
        <real>0.0</real>
        <key>max</key>
        <real>40.0</real>
        <key>showValue</key>
        <true/>
        <key>valueFormat</key>
        <string>%.0f pt</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSliderCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Move up or down</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <real>0.0</real>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadPillNudgeY</string>
        <key>min</key>
        <real>-30.0</real>
        <key>max</key>
        <real>30.0</real>
        <key>showValue</key>
        <true/>
        <key>valueFormat</key>
        <string>%.0f pt</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSGroupCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Return to Idle</string>
        <key>footerText</key>
        <string>The expanded Island goes back to idle when either limit is reached. Never means no limit. The download itself carries on, and the progress bar comes back when the next download starts. Swiping the bar away does the same. The size limit only applies to downloads that report sizes (the test download); App Store downloads report a percentage only, so use the time limit for them.</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSliderCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>After this much is downloaded</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <real>0.0</real>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadIdleAfterMB</string>
        <key>min</key>
        <real>0.0</real>
        <key>max</key>
        <real>5000.0</real>
        <key>showValue</key>
        <true/>
        <key>valueFormat</key>
        <string>%.0f MB</string>
        <key>zeroText</key>
        <string>Never</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSliderCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>After this long on screen</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <real>0.0</real>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadIdleAfterSeconds</string>
        <key>min</key>
        <real>0.0</real>
        <key>max</key>
        <real>900.0</real>
        <key>showValue</key>
        <true/>
        <key>valueFormat</key>
        <string>%.0f s</string>
        <key>zeroText</key>
        <string>Never</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSGroupCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Test Download</string>
        <key>footerText</key>
        <string>A simulated download with a changing speed, for trying the layout and the limits. Turn on Show Download Progress first. Apple Mode hides it like every other customization.</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSSliderCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Test download size</string>
        <key>default</key>
        <real>800.0</real>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
        <key>key</key>
        <string>DownloadTestSizeMB</string>
        <key>min</key>
        <real>50.0</real>
        <key>max</key>
        <real>5000.0</real>
        <key>showValue</key>
        <true/>
        <key>valueFormat</key>
        <string>%.0f MB</string>
        <key>PostNotification</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti/PrefsChanged</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSButtonCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Start Test Download</string>
        <key>action</key>
        <string>startTestDownload</string>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>cell</key>
        <string>PSButtonCell</string>
        <key>label</key>
        <string>Stop Test Download</string>
        <key>action</key>
        <string>stopTestDownload</string>
        <key>defaults</key>
        <string>com.wilburt.oiti.prefs</string>
      </dict>
    </array>
  </dict>
</plist>
